cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its benchmark data, please cite it as below."
title: "Project Janus: a contextual-bandit (LinUCB) load balancer for Kubernetes"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: tejaromalius
repository-code: "https://github.com/tejaromalius-labs/ProjectJanus"
license:
  - PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
  - CC-BY-NC-4.0
abstract: >-
  Janus is a LinUCB contextual-bandit load balancer: a Rust core wrapped by a Go
  reverse proxy. The repository includes a black-box benchmark harness and raw
  results comparing it with round robin, least connections, power of two choices
  and Peak EWMA. The results are preliminary (one campaign, one VM, synthetic
  workload); see README.md and docs/known-issues.md for their limits. Benchmark
  data and documentation are licensed CC-BY-NC-4.0 (see LICENSE-DATA).
keywords:
  - load balancing
  - contextual bandits
  - LinUCB
  - Kubernetes
